::node[study_session]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=study session, pomodoro, deep work, focus, notes, review, concentration]

::dense
Focused study session: pomodoro blocks, active-recall notes, end-of-session review.

::full
Structures a single focused study session for maximum retention and minimum cognitive
fatigue. Uses the Pomodoro technique for time-boxing, active-recall note-taking during
study, and a mandatory review ritual to consolidate memory before the session ends.

::steps
1. Pre-session setup (5 min): choose ONE topic or chapter; clear distractions; set timer.
2. Pomodoro block (25 min): read/watch/code actively. Do NOT highlight passively.
   Take margin notes as questions ("What is X? Why does Y work?").
3. Break (5 min): stand, walk, no screens. Let consolidation begin.
4. Second Pomodoro: answer the questions from block 1 from memory before re-reading.
5. After 2 Pomodoros take a longer break (15-20 min).
6. End-of-session review (10 min): write a 5-sentence summary from memory (no notes).
   Check against source; note any gaps.
7. Add new Anki cards for anything that needed checking.
8. Log: topic, duration, pages/sections covered, one key insight, one open question.

::assertions
assert session_topic != "" "A topic or chapter must be set before starting the session."

::edges
